# Video know-how: agent guide

This folder is the video know-how package: John's practice notes in two shelves, built from John's repository at commit `{{commit}}`. The [README](README.md) describes it.

- **Start**: read [video-knowhow-craft/Home.md](video-knowhow-craft/Home.md), the craft shelf. For engineering detail and the original cases, go to [video-knowhow-code/Home.md](video-knowhow-code/Home.md), the code shelf.
- **Before writing in a shelf**: read its `AGENTS.md` and `Editorial notes.md`. Follow the page and link rules in the Editorial notes' "Page format and links" section: ship only internal relative links or web links, and describe workspace material in prose. Define each term once, in `video-knowhow-code/glossary.toml`, which renders the [Glossary](video-knowhow-code/Glossary.md).
- **What to rely on**: externally documented practice and what was learned from SLASH_MY, the skills hype film, the one production John endorses. The craft shelf's generalizations, drawn from SLASH_MY, are informed interpretation and have yet to guide a production of their own. The chatlog productions and the comparison runs are records of earlier attempts, since superseded, kept as evidence and as specimens. [Content lineage](video-knowhow-code/sources/Content%20lineage.md) classifies every page.
- **After editing**: run `uv run video-knowhow-craft/tools/linkcheck.py` and `uv run video-knowhow-craft/tools/termcheck.py` from this folder, and fix every broken link and term finding. After editing glossary.toml, run `uv run video-knowhow-craft/tools/glossary.py` to rewrite the Glossary.
- **To start a production**: the starter is `video-knowhow-code/starter/`, a runnable example video built on it is `video-knowhow-code/showcase/`, the samples are `video-knowhow-code/samples/`, and the bootstrap page is `video-knowhow-code/knowledge/Production bootstrap.md`.
- **Stays in John's workspace**: the SLASH_MY production source (described in prose at snapshot `32dec413`, audio snapshots `fd543f2a` and `f7f9d199`), the motion and design reference collections (relied-on claims are inlined and the [upstream motion collection](https://github.com/gongnyang/awesome-ai-motion) is web-linked), the comparison lab (the case pages report its findings), the chatlog (the [chatlog index](video-knowhow-code/sources/Chatlog%20index.md) locates its passages), and rendered media, apart from the showcase's small review media in `video-knowhow-code/showcase/media/`.
- **Generated**: the HTML pages in `roundup/`. Edit the roundup Markdown, then run `uv run video-knowhow-craft/roundup/render_static.py` to rebuild both from it and glossary.toml.
- **Attribution**: [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md) says which material is John's and which belongs to the upstream collections and quoted sources.
